# A conforming INSTANCE of the worked example. Its profile is in grid-pair-profile.ttl.
#
# Three of the specification's gates -- test_lift, test_conformance and test_shapes -- need a
# bundle profile plus a conforming instance to exercise. They used the Shapefile profile until
# the profile library moved to its own repository, which was a dependency the wrong way round:
# a normative gate should not need a description of a third-party format to run, and could not
# be fixed without touching a file that is now someone else's to maintain.
#
# So this is a fictional two-part format with no real-world counterpart. It exercises exactly
# what the shapes need -- a naming-convention bundle, a primary part, a carried aspect, a part
# role from the register -- and nothing else, which also makes a failure point at the shape
# rather than at some incidental property of a real format.
@prefix ex:      <https://example.org/spec/bundle#> .
@prefix abnd:    <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/bundle#> .
@prefix araster: <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/raster#> .
@prefix asref:   <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#> .
@prefix afs:     <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/fsmeta#> .
@prefix rpr:     <https://hexplain.io/ns/register/part-role#> .
@prefix hexplain:<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# ---------- A conforming instance ----------
ex:sample a abnd:Asset ; dcterms:conformsTo ex:GridPair ;
    abnd:boundBy abnd:NamingConvention ; abnd:stem "sample" ;
    abnd:primaryPart ex:sample.grd ;
    abnd:hasPart ex:sample.grd , ex:sample.wld .

ex:sample.grd a abnd:Part ; abnd:partRole rpr:Payload ; afs:fileName "sample.grd" ;
    araster:width 256 ; araster:height 256 .

ex:sample.wld a abnd:Part ; abnd:partRole rpr:SpatialReference ; afs:fileName "sample.wld" ;
    asref:epsgCode 4326 .
